        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/cassandra-rs/pulls/1",
          "merged_at": "2021-11-27T05:32:38Z"
        },
        "body": "Makes cassandra-rs's session keyspace aware, such that for a \"Bound\" session, it can spit out it's keyspace name.\r\n\r\nIt accomplishes this by introducing the concept of a `SessionScope` which can be either `Bound` or `Unbound`, of which represent whether or not the session is connected to a keyspace. We encode these in types to optionally expose the `Session.keyspace()` function, and make it so that if you require a keyspace connected session (as Discord does internally w/ the `CassandraUdt` derive macro). ",
        "reactions": {
